# Project: {{PROJECT_NAME}}

## Code search

This project uses **skelesearch** — AST-aware semantic code search backed by tree-sitter
chunking and CozoDB HNSW+BM25 hybrid retrieval.

### Search

```
skelesearch search "<query>" [--limit N] [--json]
```

Results are **candidates**, not assertions. Always read the surrounding code before
concluding a function does or does not do something. False positives occur when symbol
names are similar across files.

### Index

```
skelesearch index .
```

Run after a fresh clone, after large merges, or any time search results feel stale.
The index lives in `.skelesearch/` at the project root.

### Status

```
skelesearch status --json
```

Reports `indexed_files`, `total_chunks`, `last_indexed`, `estimated_stale`, and
`watching` (true when `skelesearch watch` is running. Automatic file-change re-indexing is a v2 feature; in v1, watch mode keeps a sentinel process alive for hook detection).

### When to re-index

- After a fresh clone (no index exists yet).
- After rebasing or merging large changesets.
- When `estimated_stale` from `status --json` is high.
- The `post-edit-reindex` hook handles incremental re-indexing automatically
  when skelesearch is wired via the Claude Code plugin.

## MCP tools (when running as MCP server)

| Tool | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `search_code` | Hybrid BM25+dense search; returns ranked chunks |
| `smart_search` | Classifies query and selects best retrieval strategy — prefer this for ambiguous queries |
| `find_symbol` | Look up function/struct/type definitions by exact or partial name |
| `index_codebase` | Trigger indexing from within a Claude session |
| `index_status` | Check whether the index is current |
| `get_file_context` | Retrieve all chunks and import edges for a specific file |

Start with `smart_search` when you are unsure which strategy fits. Fall back to
`search_code` with `include_graph: true` to pull in import-graph neighbours.

If the project is not yet indexed, call `index_codebase` with the project root path
before running any search tool.

For MCP server setup, see `docs/quickstart.md`.
